{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>A burnt offering and sacrifices to Elohim.</b> As a sign of accepting the yoke of His kingdom, as in the case of Naaman, who said: כִּי לֹא יַעֲשֶׂה עוֹד עַבְדְּךָ עֹלָה וּמִנְחָה לֵאלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים כִּי אִם לַה' (2 Kings 5:17)." "<b>To eat bread with Moses' father-in-law.</b> To rejoice with him over his having come under the wings of the Shekhinah, as it says: יִשְׂמַח יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּעֹשָׂיו (Psalms 149:2)." "<b>Before Elohim.</b> Before the altar upon which those sacrifices were offered — whether that altar was the one Moses built at the defeat of Amalek, or whether it was another not mentioned by name. And their eating of the sacrifices was before the altar, in the manner of those things eaten within the curtains."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:07.610144962Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}